.TH RP 1 "2026-07-09" "reta arch mojo" "Reta commands"
.SH NAME
rp \- start the interactive Reta prompt in vi mode with logging
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rp
.RI [ prompt-options ]
.PP
.B rp
.B -befehl
.RI command ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rp
starts the interactive Reta prompt profile.  It is the convenient prompt
frontend for repeatedly entering short Reta commands, numeric commands and full
.B reta
command lines.
.PP
The historical
.B rp
profile uses vi-style editing and has command logging enabled by default.  It
shares the native prompt execution library with
.BR rpl ,
.B rpe
and
.BR rpb ;
interactive input is handled only by the interactive prompt library.
.SH PROMPT OPTIONS
.TP
.B -vi
Use vi mode instead of Emacs-style editing.
.TP
.B -log
Enable prompt command-history logging at startup.
.TP
.B -language=LANGUAGE
Select the prompt language.  Accepted aliases include
.BR deutsch ,
.BR german ,
.BR english ,
.BR englisch ,
.BR vietnamese ,
.BR vietnamesisch ,
.BR chinese ,
.B chinesisch
and Korean aliases.
.TP
.B -debug
Enable developer debug output.
.TP
.B -befehl
Execute one prompt command built from the remaining arguments and exit.
.TP
.B -e
Apply the compact/no-empty-output command modifier to prompt commands where the
historical prompt allows it.
.TP
.BR -h , " " -help
Show prompt help.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
The prompt accepts short output commands such as
.BR a ,
.BR u ,
.BR t ,
.BR p ,
.BR prim ,
.BR multis ,
.BR modulo ,
.BR mond ,
.BR alles ,
.BR primzahlkreuz ,
.BR richtung
and full
.B reta
commands.
.PP
.BR q ,
.BR :q ,
.BR exit ,
.B quit
and
.B ende
leave the prompt.
.PP
.B shell
runs a shell command,
.B python
runs a Python command and
.B math
runs a Python-style calculation command.
.SH STORAGE COMMANDS
.TP
.B S
Store the next command.  Repeating
.B S
extends the stored command sequence.
.TP
.B s
Store the previous command.
.TP
.B o
Print or apply the stored command.  Pressing Enter alone can also use the stored
command.
.TP
.B l
Open deletion of stored commands by selection.
.SH ROW EXPRESSIONS
Prompt row expressions follow the same numeric language as
.BR reta :
.BR 2 ,
.BR 3-5 ,
.BR 2,3-5 ,
.BR 5+2+4 ,
.BR v20-22 ,
.BR -20,v10 ,
.BR 1/2,3 ,
.B 1/2-3/3
and similar fraction ranges are accepted by supported commands.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/rp
Default public executable for a standard installation.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_prompt_interactive_mojo.so
Interactive prompt input/session library used by
.BR rp ,
.B rpl
and
.BR rpe .
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/reta/libreta_prompt_mojo.so
Shared prompt execution library.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start the interactive prompt:
.PP
.nf
rp
.fi
.PP
Run one command and exit:
.PP
.nf
rp -befehl prim 60
.fi
.PP
Inside the prompt, print the prime factorisation of 60:
.PP
.nf
prim 60
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR reta (1),
.BR rpl (1),
.BR rpe (1),
.BR rpb (1)
